WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.880
- [Narrator] Although there
are many castles in Germany,

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.389
there's none quite like Eltz Castle.

00:00:05.389 --> 00:00:10.223
It has been privately owned
by the Eltz family since 1157.

00:00:16.589 --> 00:00:19.560
The Eltz Castle was originally constructed

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.930
in the 11th century.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.780
However, additions and restorations

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.333
have been made over the years.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.780
Unlike most castles, Eltz
Castle isn't easy to spot.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.250
It sits off the main road,

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.480
high on a rock within a low valley

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.220
and is surrounded by a lush forest.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.590
Many visitors are drawn
to the hiking trails

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.403
surrounding the castle grounds.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.380
Thirty-four generations of the Eltz family

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.630
have lived among the castle's 120 rooms.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:51.240
And since today, no one in the
family lives there full time,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.863
the ancestral home is open to the public.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.540
Every year over 300,000 visitors

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.870
come to see the castle
and its armory, treasury

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.073
and original furnishings that
are over eight centuries old.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.200
Throughout Europe's tumultuous history,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.600
this enchanting castle was
never invaded or destroyed.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.650
Its rich history has earned it a spot

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:14.890
on the 500 Deutsche Mark note,

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:16.810
making it a special sight for those

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.073
who get to experience it in person.

